description:
Design a circuit that computes the absolute value of a complex number represented by its real (y_re) and imaginary (y_im) parts, both 13 bits in width and signed. The module processes these inputs to derive the absolute value by first calculating the non-negative magnitudes of the real and imaginary components, then performing a series of conditional assignments and arithmetic operations to determine the overall magnitude, which is output as y_abs. The implementation ensures that the results are consistently calculated as signed values, ultimately providing the absolute value of the complex number.
module top_module(
	input signed [12:0] y_re, y_im,
	output signed [12:0] y_abs
);

code:
module top_module(
	input signed [12:0] y_re, y_im,
	output signed [12:0] y_abs
);wire signed [12:0] a, b;
	assign a=(y_re<0)?(-y_re):y_re;
	assign b=(y_im<0)?(-y_im):y_im;


	wire signed [12:0] m1;
	assign m1=(a>b)?(a-{3'b000,a[10:3]}):(b-{3'b000,b[10:3]});


	wire signed [12:0] m2;
	assign m2=(a<b)?{1'b0,a[12:1]}:{1'b0,b[12:1]};


	wire signed [12:0] m3;
	assign m3=(a>b)?a:b;

	assign y_abs=((m1+m2)>m3)?(m1+m2):m3;

endmodule

