description:
Implement a debounce circuit that stabilizes a noisy input signal. The module samples the input (IN) at each rising edge of the clock and maintains a shift register to track the last M samples. If all samples in the shift register are LOW, the output (OUT) is set to LOW; if all samples are HIGH, OUT is set to HIGH. This design effectively filters out spurious fluctuations in the input signal, ensuring that the output reflects a stable and clean signal transition.
module top_module(
    input wire clock,
    input wire IN,
    output reg OUT
);

code:
module top_module(
    input wire clock,
    input wire IN,
    output reg OUT
);parameter M = 8;
 reg [M-1:0]shift;


 always @ (posedge clock) 
 begin
   shift[M-1:0] <= {shift[M-2:0],IN}; 

   if(~|shift)
     OUT <= 1'b0;

   else if(&shift)
     OUT <= 1'b1;
   else OUT <= OUT;
 end
 endmodule

